  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Nusantara AI Architecture**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the architecture for Nusantara AI. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the `E2EEncryptionManager`. My current plan is to use AES-256-GCM symmetric encryption for data protection, and use PBKDF2/SHA-256 for key derivation combined with some form of device unique identifier.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Management Scope**\n\nI\'m now integrating ideas related to a simulated keystore and client keypair, including a privacy mode indicator. I am designing features like zero-log certification, ephemeral session toggles, and local key export/wipe capabilities. I am also planning an in-app encrypted/decrypted inspector tool for real-time visualization. I\'m focusing on defining the database and persistence layer details, especially around entity structures. I am building entities for chat sessions, messages, personas, analytics logs, and documents.\n\n\n**Defining AI Engine Integration**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the design of the Hybrid AI Engine. I\'m building out the functionality for both online (Gemini API) and offline modes, including model configurations. I\'m also working on the logic for the hybrid auto-switching mechanism based on connectivity, and designing the sync manager to handle interactions.\n\n\n**Designing App Screens**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the app\'s structure, focusing on the main navigation. The bottom bar will feature a \"Chat & Reasoning\" section with a dynamic model selector, a mode switch for online/offline/hybrid, and enhancements for chain-of-thought and code rendering. I\'m also including a \"Multimodal Studio\" for image analysis and generation, and a \"Flow Debate Arena\". Lastly, I am building an analytics dashboard to track personal efficiency metrics.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 501063313
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
